  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Flood Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 13 August continuous rainfall in north and north-eastern Bangladesh, together with the onrush of water from upstream, have caused flash floods in low-lying and densely populated areas. 
More than 800,000 people have been affected, including 500,000 displaced (ACAPS briefing note, 27.08.2014). 
Caritas Bangladesh has conducted a brief needs assessment in Sirajganj district, where a reported 48,000 households have been affected (CB assessment, 27.8.2014). Following the result of the needs assessment, Caritas Bangladesh plans to undertake immediate emergency relief for 1,000 families who have been severely impacted by the flooding. The emergency relief will provide the 1,000 families with supplementary food for up to 15 days, cash support for essential household items and Cash for Work for ongoing support to 500 people whose livelihoods have been disrupted. The project will work in 4 unions in 2 sub-districts of Sirajganj. The project will be completed within 45 days of the start date.
.</narrative>
  </description>
